---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Demo from '../components/Demo.astro';
import FrameworkPicker from '../components/FrameworkPicker.astro';
import Fw from '../components/Fw.astro';
import { DOCS, url } from '../lib/site';
import { GCDS_VERSION } from '../lib/versions';

const cdn = `https://cdn.design-system.canada.ca/@gcds-core`;
---

<Base title="Set up your project" current="setup">
  <gcds-text>
    These steps are the same as the
    <gcds-link href={`${DOCS}/start-to-use/develop/`}>install instructions in the GCDS documentation</gcds-link>.
    Once you’re done, check that it worked.
  </gcds-text>

  <FrameworkPicker />

  <!-- Step wording below matches design-system.canada.ca/en/start-to-use/develop/<framework>/ -->

  <!-- ---------------- HTML ---------------- -->
  <Fw for="html">
    <gcds-heading tag="h2">1. Install the package</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>Navigate to your project’s root folder and run the following command:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npm install @gcds-core/components`} />

    <gcds-heading tag="h2">2. Include GC Design System in your project</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>
      Add the following <code>link</code> tags inside the <code>head</code> tag of your <code>HTML</code> files to load
      GC Design System:
    </gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`<!-- GC Design System -->
<link
  rel="stylesheet"
  href="/node_modules/@gcds-core/components/dist/gcds/gcds.css"
/>
<script
  type="module"
  src="/node_modules/@gcds-core/components/dist/gcds/gcds.esm.js"
></script>`}
    />

    <gcds-details details-title="Can’t use npm? Use the CDN">
      <gcds-text>
        Add the following code to the <code>head</code> tag of your <code>HTML</code> files to load GC Design System.
        Make sure the current version is listed.
      </gcds-text>
      <gcds-text>Current version: Version {GCDS_VERSION}.</gcds-text>
      <CodeBlock
        code={`<!-- GC Design System -->
<link
  rel="stylesheet"
  href="${cdn}/components@${GCDS_VERSION}/dist/gcds/gcds.css"
/>
<script
  type="module"
  src="${cdn}/components@${GCDS_VERSION}/dist/gcds/gcds.esm.js"
></script>`}
      />
      <gcds-text>
        The code will remain unchanged until you manually update the version in the CDN URLs. This is ideal for
        production environments.
      </gcds-text>
      <gcds-text margin-bottom="0">
        Check for new GC Design System versions regularly to update the latest pinned version.
      </gcds-text>
    </gcds-details>

    <gcds-notice class="mt-500" notice-role="info" notice-title="Viewing your page locally" notice-title-tag="h3">
      <gcds-text margin-bottom="0">
        <code>&lt;script type="module"&gt;</code> requires a server to load properly. Run a local server from your
        project’s root folder, for example <code>npx serve .</code>, instead of opening the file directly.
      </gcds-text>
    </gcds-notice>
  </Fw>

  <!-- ---------------- React ---------------- -->
  <Fw for="react">
    <gcds-heading tag="h2">1. Install the package</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>Navigate to your project’s root folder and run the following command:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npm install @gcds-core/components @gcds-core/components-react`} />

    <gcds-heading tag="h2">2. Import GC Design System</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>
      Place the following code in the <code>index.js</code> file of your app to import GC Design System styles:
    </gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock lang="js" code={`import '@gcds-core/components-react/gcds.css';`} />
  </Fw>

  <!-- ---------------- Vue ---------------- -->
  <Fw for="vue">
    <gcds-heading tag="h2">1. Install the package</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>Navigate to your project’s root folder and run the following command:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npm install @gcds-core/components-vue`} />

    <gcds-heading tag="h2">2. Import GC Design System</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>In your <code>main.js</code> file, import the GC Design System components plugin and use it:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="js"
      code={`import { GcdsComponents } from '@gcds-core/components-vue';

createApp(App).use(GcdsComponents).mount('#app');`}
    />

    <gcds-heading tag="h2">3. Import GC Design System styles</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>There are 2 ways to do this:</gcds-text>
    <ul class="list-disc mb-300">
      <li><gcds-text margin-bottom="100">Import styles to <code>main.js</code>.</gcds-text></li>
      <li><gcds-text margin-bottom="100">Import styles to <code>App.vue</code>.</gcds-text></li>
    </ul>
    <gcds-text>a. Import the styles to your <code>main.js</code> file, alongside your <code>style.css</code>:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="js"
      code={`import '@gcds-core/components-vue/gcds.css';
import './style.css';`}
    />
    <gcds-text>b. Import the styles to your <code>App.vue</code> using the HTML <code>style</code> tag:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="vue"
      code={`<style src="@gcds-core/components-vue/gcds.css">
  /* global styles */
</style>`}
    />
  </Fw>

  <!-- ---------------- Angular ---------------- -->
  <Fw for="angular">
    <gcds-heading tag="h2">1. Install the package</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>Navigate to your project’s root folder and run the following command:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npm install @gcds-core/components @gcds-core/components-angular`} />

    <gcds-heading tag="h2">2. Import GC Design System</gcds-heading>
    <gcds-text>Place the following code in the <code>app.module.ts</code> file of your app:</gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="ts"
      code={`import { GcdsComponentsModule } from '@gcds-core/components-angular';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    ...
  ],
  imports: [
    ...,
    GcdsComponentsModule
  ],
  providers: [],
  bootstrap: [...]
})
export class AppModule { }`}
    />
    <gcds-details details-title="Using standalone components?">
      <gcds-text>
        New Angular projects (version 19 and later) use standalone components by default and don’t have an
        <code>app.module.ts</code>. Add <code>GcdsComponentsModule</code> to the <code>imports</code> of each
        component that uses GC Design System instead:
      </gcds-text>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="ts"
        code={`import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { GcdsComponentsModule } from '@gcds-core/components-angular';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  imports: [GcdsComponentsModule],
  templateUrl: './app.component.html',
})
export class AppComponent {}`}
      />
    </gcds-details>
    <gcds-text>
      Place the following code in the <code>styles.scss</code> file of your app to import GC Design System styles:
    </gcds-text>
    <CodeBlock lang="scss" code={`@import '../node_modules/@gcds-core/components/dist/gcds/gcds.css';`} />
  </Fw>

  <!-- ---------------- All ---------------- -->
  <gcds-heading tag="h2">Check that it worked</gcds-heading>
  <gcds-text>
    Add the following code to your page and load it in the browser. You should see the same button:
  </gcds-text>
  <Demo html={`<gcds-button type="button">It works</gcds-button>`} />

  <gcds-checkboxes
    name="setup-checklist"
    legend="Setup checklist"
    hint="For your own tracking. Tick each one off as you go."
    options={JSON.stringify([
      { id: 'chk-install', label: 'Installed the package (or added the CDN links)', value: 'install' },
      { id: 'chk-import', label: 'Imported GC Design System and its styles', value: 'import' },
      { id: 'chk-button', label: 'Saw a styled GCDS button in my browser', value: 'button' },
    ])}
  ></gcds-checkboxes>

  <gcds-heading tag="h3">If something looks wrong</gcds-heading>
  <gcds-details details-title="I see plain text instead of a button">
    <gcds-text>
      The components aren’t registered. In HTML, check the <code>&lt;script type="module"&gt;</code> tag loaded
      (look for a 404 in the browser’s Network tab) and that you’re using a local server, not <code>file://</code>.
      In a framework, check the import from step 2.
    </gcds-text>
  </gcds-details>
  <gcds-details details-title="The button is there but the fonts or spacing look off">
    <gcds-text margin-bottom="0">
      <code>gcds.css</code> isn’t loaded. It contains the fonts, design tokens and base styles that the components rely
      on. Load it once, globally, before your own styles.
    </gcds-text>
  </gcds-details>
  <gcds-details details-title="My framework says it doesn’t know the element">
    <ul class="list-disc">
      <li><gcds-text margin-bottom="100"><strong>Angular:</strong> the component using the tag needs <code>GcdsComponentsModule</code> in its <code>imports</code>.</gcds-text></li>
      <li><gcds-text margin-bottom="100"><strong>Vue:</strong> check that <code>.use(GcdsComponents)</code> runs before <code>.mount()</code>.</gcds-text></li>
      <li><gcds-text margin-bottom="0"><strong>React:</strong> import the PascalCase component (<code>GcdsButton</code>) instead of writing <code>&lt;gcds-button&gt;</code>.</gcds-text></li>
    </ul>
  </gcds-details>

  <gcds-heading tag="h2">Want a head start?</gcds-heading>
  <gcds-notice notice-role="info" notice-title="New: GCDS starter apps" notice-title-tag="h3">
    <gcds-text margin-bottom="0">
      The starter app tool creates a new project with GCDS already set up. You choose a folder and a framework,
      and it does the rest. We still recommend doing the setup by hand once so you know what’s going on. Then use
      the starter app for real projects. See <gcds-link href={url('next-steps')}>next steps</gcds-link>.
    </gcds-text>
  </gcds-notice>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`npm create @gcds-core/app@latest`} />

  <gcds-text margin-top="400">
    Full instructions for each framework are on the
    <gcds-link href={`${DOCS}/start-to-use/develop/`}>GCDS developer documentation</gcds-link>.
  </gcds-text>
</Base>
